# Known violations of the CSS architecture contract (web/css/README.md).
#
# Format: <check> <item>   # optional note
#
# This file is the outstanding debt of the CSS restructure. Entries may be
# removed, never added: a new violation is a build failure, and an entry that
# stops matching anything is also a failure, so the file cannot rot.
#
# The ownership block arrived in one go when the sheets were split and every
# `"owns": ["*"]` became a real list of roots. Until then the check could not
# see anything — one file owning everything cannot misfile a rule. Nothing got
# worse that day; the debt simply became countable. It only shrinks from here.
#
# Audit what is still owed:  node scripts/lint-css-arch --emit-allowlist

